"answer": "The emails regarding Q2 budget revisions include: 1) Oliver Grant (Project Manager) reported that capital expenditure projects (new office building and IT infrastructure upgrade) came in 10% over budget, requiring fund reallocation. 2) Karen Smith (CFO) revised the Q2 budget by shifting funds to emerging market bonds, resulting in a revised profit forecast of $9.378 million, a 3.5% increase. 3) Emily Rogers (Operations Manager) requested approval for an unplanned $50,000 IT security expenditure that will affect the Q2 budget. 4) Diana Wells (Chief Auditor) noted that the upcoming Q2 audit will require accurate records of recent budget revisions. 5) A team communication emphasized the need to finalize Q2 budget estimations, noting a Q1 profit of $5 million, and requested the estimated Q2 profit figure be communicated to the CFO."
